# llama-toolchest environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env and edit as needed:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# If you use ./setup.sh install, the .env file is generated automatically.
# Edit .env directly to change settings without re-running setup.

# ─── Port configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host ports for the llama-toolchest services. The container listens
# internally on 3000 (UI) and 8080 (inference) — these settings control which
# host ports map to them. Change these if the defaults conflict with other
# services.

LLAMA_TOOLCHEST_PORT=3000
LLAMA_TOOLCHEST_INFERENCE_PORT=8080

# ─── Secure install (Caddy reverse proxy) ────────────────────────────────────
# Written automatically by `./setup.sh install --secure`. Do not hand-edit
# unless you know what you're doing — see docs/secure.md. In secure mode the
# app binds to loopback (LLAMA_TOOLCHEST_BIND) and Caddy publishes 80/443/8080.
#
# LLAMA_TOOLCHEST_SECURE=1                       # stack docker-compose.secure.yml
# LLAMA_TOOLCHEST_BIND=127.0.0.1:                # interface prefix for app ports
# LLAMA_TOOLCHEST_EXTERNAL_URL=https://host      # makes UI links render over HTTPS
# CADDY_HTTP_PORT=80
# CADDY_HTTPS_PORT=443
# CADDY_CHAT_PORT=8080
# (admin username + bcrypt hash live in ./Caddyfile, not here)

# ─── Model storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mount a host directory for model storage so models survive container/volume
# removal. Leave commented out to store models in the Docker volume.
# The directory will be created if it doesn't exist.
#LLAMA_TOOLCHEST_MODELS_DIR=/home/user/llm-models

# ─── AMD ROCm settings (only needed for AMD GPUs) ────────────────────────────
# These are auto-detected by setup.sh. Only set manually if auto-detection
# gets it wrong or you're not using setup.sh.

# HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION — Override the GPU architecture reported to ROCm.
# Only needed for GPUs not natively supported by ROCm (e.g. RDNA 1, Vega).
# Examples: 10.1.0 (RDNA 1), 9.0.0 (Vega)
# Leave commented out for RDNA 2/3/4 GPUs.
#HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=

# Host group IDs for GPU device access inside the container.
# Find yours with: getent group video | cut -d: -f3
#                  getent group render | cut -d: -f3
#HOST_VIDEO_GID=
#HOST_RENDER_GID=

# ROCM_VARIANT — which ROCm container to build (AMD, container mode).
#   stable  Dockerfile.rocm — ROCm 7.2.4 on Fedora. The tested default.
#   next    Dockerfile.rocm-next — built on AMD's own ROCm image, which is the
#           only way to get ROCm 10: repo.radeon.com has no 10.x packages.
#           Needs a host kernel of 6.14 or newer for the AMD driver.
# setup.sh writes this from the choice made at install time. Editing it here
# takes effect on the next ./setup.sh rebuild. Switching versions means
# rebuilding your llama.cpp builds — nothing is deleted, so switching back
# makes the old ones work again.
#ROCM_VARIANT=stable

# ROCM_BASE_IMAGE — the ROCm release used when ROCM_VARIANT=next. A bare tag is
# looked up in docker.io/rocm/dev-ubuntu-24.04; a full reference is used as
# given. Tags: https://hub.docker.com/r/rocm/dev-ubuntu-24.04/tags
#ROCM_BASE_IMAGE=10.0.0-full
